<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">17 March in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">8 events that happened on 17 March, from 45 BCE to 1958.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">45 BCE <span class="tih-ago">2,070 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Julius Caesar defeats the Pompeian army at the Battle of Munda</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">In southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/julius-caesar">Julius Caesar</a> defeated the Pompeian army of Gnaeus and Sextus Pompeius and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/titus-labienus">Titus Labienus</a>. Labienus was killed and Gnaeus Pompeius was caught and executed soon afterwards; it was Caesar's last battle of the civil war.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-munda">Battle of Munda</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/julius-caesar">Julius Caesar</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/titus-labienus">Titus Labienus</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">461 CE <span class="tih-ago">1,565 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Traditional date of the death of Saint Patrick</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">By tradition Patrick, the Romano-British missionary to Ireland, died on 17 March, though the year is uncertain. His feast became Ireland's national day, celebrated by the Irish diaspora worldwide.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1337">1337 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">689 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Edward the Black Prince receives the Duchy of Cornwall</h2><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/edward-the-black-prince">Edward the Black Prince</a>, eldest son of King Edward III, received the Duchy of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cornwall">Cornwall</a> by a royal charter, having been made duke in parliament in February. It was the earliest creation of a duke in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/england">England</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/edward-the-black-prince">Edward the Black Prince</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/boston" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/boston.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1776">1776 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">250 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">British troops evacuate Boston</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">After Washington fortified Dorchester Heights with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/field-artillery">cannon</a> hauled from Fort Ticonderoga, General Howe's army sailed for Halifax. The siege of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/boston">Boston</a> ended in an American success.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/boston">Boston</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1845">1845 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">181 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Stephen Perry patents the rubber band</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Stephen <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/matthew-c-perry">Perry</a> of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/london">London</a> firm Messrs Perry and Co patented bands made of vulcanised <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rubber">rubber</a> for holding papers together. The humble invention became universal.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/london">London</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1905">1905 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">121 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Einstein completes his paper on light quanta</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Einstein finished a paper proposing that light comes in discrete packets of energy, explaining the photoelectric effect. It helped found <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/quantum-mechanics">quantum theory</a> and earned him the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nobel-prize">Nobel Prize</a>.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1948">1948 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">78 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Brussels Treaty creates a Western European defence pact</h2><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/belgium">Belgium</a>, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-the-netherlands">Netherlands</a> and Luxembourg agreed to defend one another against attack. The pact paved the way for <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nato">NATO</a> in 1949 and later became the Western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/european-union">European Union</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/european-union">European Union</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/belgium">Belgium</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1958">1958 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">68 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">US launches Vanguard 1 satellite</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The grapefruit-sized satellite, mocked by Khrushchev, showed that the Earth is slightly pear-shaped. Long silent, it is the oldest human-made object still in orbit.</p></div></li></ol>
<section class="day-ppl" aria-labelledby="day-born"><h2 class="ref-sec-title" id="day-born">Born on 17 March <span class="n">3</span></h2><ul class="enc-seealso"><li><a href="/encyclopedia/james-iv-of-scotland"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/james-iv-of-scotland.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">James IV of Scotland</span><span class="tp">1473–1513</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/gottlieb-daimler"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/gottlieb-daimler.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Gottlieb Daimler</span><span class="tp">1834–1900</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/sheikh-mujibur-rahman"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/sheikh-mujibur-rahman.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Sheikh Mujibur Rahman</span><span class="tp">1920–1975</span></span></a></li></ul></section>
<section class="day-ppl" aria-labelledby="day-died"><h2 class="ref-sec-title" id="day-died">Died on 17 March <span class="n">7</span></h2><ul class="enc-seealso"><li><a href="/encyclopedia/titus-labienus"><span class="ph ph-person" aria-hidden="true"></span><span><span class="nm">Titus Labienus</span><span class="tp">c. 100–45 BCE</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/harold-harefoot"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/harold-harefoot.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Harold Harefoot</span><span class="tp">c. 1016–1040</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/lulach"><span class="ph ph-person" aria-hidden="true"></span><span><span class="nm">Lulach</span><span class="tp">d. 1058</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/ibn-khaldun"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/ibn-khaldun.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Ibn Khaldun</span><span class="tp">1332–1406</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/jules-ferry"><span class="ph ph-person" aria-hidden="true"></span><span><span class="nm">Jules Ferry</span><span class="tp">1832–1893</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/ramon-magsaysay"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/ramon-magsaysay.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Ramon Magsaysay</span><span class="tp">1907–1957</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/john-magufuli"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/john-magufuli.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">John Magufuli</span><span class="tp">1959–2021</span></span></a></li></ul></section>
<p class="day-ppl-note">Dates as the sources give them: in the Julian calendar before 1582, and in some countries for longer (Britain until 1752, Russia until 1918). Only people whose day of birth or death the records agree on are listed.</p>
